# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Answer keys must NEVER be committed. See MODERNIZATION-PLAN.md section 3b.
# These files contain graded assignment/quiz answers AND document the honeypot
# design used across psyc790, data2, and psyc894 -- publishing them would
# defeat that mechanism for all three courses.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source files...
*_key.qmd
*_Key.qmd
**/keys/

# ...and every rendered artifact derived from them. The .qmd rule alone is NOT
# enough: quarto writes the fully rendered answers (and the honeypot markers)
# into _freeze/ and _site/, which would otherwise be committed.
*_key.*
*_Key.*
*_key/
*_Key/

# archive/ is legacy source excluded from the render (see _quarto.yml). Nothing
# under it should ever be frozen or published.
_freeze/archive/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course readings are copyrighted textbook chapters and live on Canvas, behind
# authentication. They must never be committed here -- this repo is public and
# is published to GitHub Pages. Link to Canvas instead. See section 7.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf
*.epub
*.docx
*.pptx
readings/

# Written by A/03/b_Slides.qmd as a live demo of write_csv()
A/03/gradebook.csv
